IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-interpretation-time`

-- Part VII, Division 2 of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Statutory instruments, sections 63 to 66.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- Section 63B (commencement of subordinate legislation) is in nt-interpretation-time.l4.
-- The days on which the Legislative Assembly sits are a fact of its calendar and are an input (sitting days: section 17).
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Section 63: regulations`

-- A regulation must, as soon as practicable after it is made, be published on the legislation website and notified in the Gazette.
-- "As soon as practicable" is a judgment the text leaves open: it is an input.
-- src:770 | If an Act contains a power to make regulations, a regulation made under that power must:
-- src:771 | (a) as soon as practicable after it is made:
-- src:772 | (i) be published on the legislation website; and
-- src:773 | (ii) be notified in the Gazette; and
@ref s 63(a) (src:770-773)
GIVEN `it has been published on the legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both were done as soon as practicable after it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(a): the regulation has been published and notified as required` MEANS
    JUST (`it has been published on the legislation website` AND `it has been notified in the Gazette` AND `both were done as soon as practicable after it was made`)

-- The regulation must, within 6 sitting days after it is made, be tabled in the Legislative Assembly.
-- The last day for tabling is the 6th sitting day after the day it is made (section 28(1) leaves out the day it is made).
-- src:774 | (b) within 6 sitting days after it is made, be tabled in the Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 63(b) (src:774)
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation is made` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 63(b): the last day on which the regulation must be tabled` MEANS
    `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after` `the day on which the regulation is made` 6 `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

@ref s 63(b) (src:774)
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the regulation is tabled` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63(b): the regulation is tabled within 6 sitting days after it is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 63(b): the last day on which the regulation must be tabled` `the day on which the regulation is made` `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (Day `the day on which the regulation is tabled` AT MOST Day last)

§ `Section 63A: rules and by-laws`

-- A rule or by-law must be signed by the person making it or, where the maker is a statutory corporation or a local government council, by a person the corporation or council authorises to sign it.
-- src:776 | (1) If an Act contains a power to make rules or by-laws, a rule or by‑law made under that power must be:
-- src:777 | (a) signed by:
-- src:778 | (i) the person making it; or
-- src:779 | (ii) if the person making it is a statutory corporation or a local government council – a person authorised by the corporation or council to sign it; and
@ref s 63A(1)(a) (src:776-779)
GIVEN `the person making it is a statutory corporation or a local government council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the person making it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by a person authorised by the corporation or council to sign it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(1)(a): the rule or by-law is signed as required` MEANS
    IF   `the person making it is a statutory corporation or a local government council`
    THEN JUST `it is signed by a person authorised by the corporation or council to sign it`
    ELSE JUST `it is signed by the person making it`

-- Once signed, it must be given to the minister administering the provision containing the power; this does not apply to a by-law under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975.
-- src:780 | (b) once signed, given to the minister administering the provision containing the power.
@ref s 63A(1)(b) (src:780)
GIVEN `it is a by-law made under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(1)(b): the signed rule or by-law must be given to the minister administering the provision containing the power` MEANS
    JUST (NOT `it is a by-law made under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975`)

-- Subsection (1)(b) does not apply to a by-law made under either of the two Unit Titles Acts.
-- src:791 | (6) Subsection (1)(b) does not apply to a by-law made under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975.
@ref s 63A(6) (src:791)
GIVEN `it is a by-law made under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(6): subsection (1)(b) applies to the by-law` MEANS
    JUST (NOT `it is a by-law made under the Unit Title Schemes Act 2009 or the Unit Titles Act 1975`)

-- The minister must, as soon as practicable after the rule or by-law is made, cause it to be published and notified in the Gazette.
-- src:781 | (2) Subject to this section, if a signed rule or by-law is given to a minister under subsection (1), that minister must:
-- src:782 | (a) as soon as practicable after it is made, cause it to be:
-- src:783 | (i) published; and
-- src:784 | (ii) notified in the Gazette; and
-- src:785 | (b) within 6 sitting days after it is notified in the Gazette, cause it to be tabled in the Legislative Assembly.
@ref s 63A(2)(a) (src:781-785)
GIVEN `the signed rule or by-law has been given to the minister under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minister has caused it to be published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minister has caused it to be notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both were done as soon as practicable after it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(2)(a): the minister has caused the rule or by-law to be published and notified as required` MEANS
    IF   `the signed rule or by-law has been given to the minister under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST (`the minister has caused it to be published` AND `the minister has caused it to be notified in the Gazette` AND `both were done as soon as practicable after it was made`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The minister must, within 6 sitting days after the rule or by-law is notified in the Gazette, cause it to be tabled.
@ref s 63A(2)(b) (src:785)
GIVEN `the day on which it is notified in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 63A(2)(b): the last day on which the rule or by-law must be tabled` MEANS
    `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after` `the day on which it is notified in the Gazette` 6 `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

-- The minister may, before the rule or by-law is notified in the Gazette, return it to the person who signed it with a request for any amendment the minister recommends.
-- src:786 | (3) If a rule or by-law is given to a minister under subsection (1)(b), the minister may, before is it notified in the Gazette, return it to the person who signed it with a request for any amendment the minister recommends.
@ref s 63A(3) (src:786)
GIVEN `it has been given to the minister under subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has not yet been notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(3): the minister may return the rule or by-law with a request for amendment` MEANS
    JUST (`it has been given to the minister under subsection (1)(b)` AND `it has not yet been notified in the Gazette`)

-- If the minister returns it, the person making it must consider the amendment and give it back to the minister, signed, with or without the amendment.
-- src:787 | (4) If a minister returns a rule or by-law under subsection (3), the person making the rule or by-law must:
-- src:788 | (a) consider the amendment; and
-- src:789 | (b) give the rule or by-law, signed in accordance with subsection (1)(a), to the minister, with or without the amendment included.
@ref s 63A(4) (src:787-789)
GIVEN `the minister has returned the rule or by-law under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making it has considered the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making it has given it back to the minister, signed in accordance with subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(4): the person making the rule or by-law has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF   `the minister has returned the rule or by-law under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST (`the person making it has considered the amendment` AND `the person making it has given it back to the minister, signed in accordance with subsection (1)(a)`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (2) applies to a rule or by-law given to the minister under subsection (4)(b).
-- src:790 | (5) Subsection (2) applies to a rule or by-law given to the minister under subsection (4)(b).
@ref s 63A(5) (src:790)
GIVEN `it was given to the minister under subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63A(5): subsection (2) applies to the rule or by-law` MEANS
    IF `it was given to the minister under subsection (4)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 63C: tabling and disallowance`

-- A failure to table subordinate legislation does not affect its validity, but may be the subject of a referral by the Assembly to the committee responsible for the examination of instruments of a legislative character or another committee.
-- src:805 | (1) A failure to table subordinate legislation in the Legislative Assembly does not affect the validity of the subordinate legislation, but may be the subject of a referral by the Assembly to the committee responsible for the examination of instruments of a legislative character or another committee of the Assembly.
@ref s 63C(1) (src:805)
GIVEN `the subordinate legislation was not tabled in the Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63C(1): the failure to table affects whether the subordinate legislation has effect` MEANS
    IF `the subordinate legislation was not tabled in the Legislative Assembly` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- The Assembly may pass a resolution disallowing subordinate legislation, or specified provisions of it, that is required to be tabled under this Division, whether or not it has been tabled.
-- src:806 | (2) The Legislative Assembly may pass a resolution disallowing subordinate legislation, or specified provisions of it, that is required to be tabled under this Division, whether or not it has been tabled.
@ref s 63C(2) (src:806)
GIVEN `the subordinate legislation is required to be tabled under Division 2 of Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been tabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63C(2): the Legislative Assembly may pass a resolution disallowing the subordinate legislation or specified provisions of it` MEANS
    IF `the subordinate legislation is required to be tabled under Division 2 of Part VII`
    THEN CONSIDER `it has been tabled`
         WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Notice of the resolution must be given within 12 sitting days after the subordinate legislation is tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b),
-- or, if it has not been tabled in accordance with them, within 12 sitting days after the last sitting day it was required to be tabled.
-- src:807 | (3) Notice of a resolution referred to in subsection (2) must be given within:
-- src:808 | (a) in the case of subordinate legislation that is tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b) – 12 sitting days after the subordinate legislation is tabled; or
-- src:809 | (b) in the case of subordinate legislation that has not been tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b) – 12 sitting days after the last sitting day the subordinate legislation was required to be tabled.
@ref s 63C(3) (src:807-809)
GIVEN `it was tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which it was tabled` IS A DATE
      `the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 63C(3): the last day on which notice of the resolution must be given` MEANS
    IF   `it was tabled in accordance with section 63(b) or 63A(2)(b)`
    THEN `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after` `the day on which it was tabled` 12 `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`
    ELSE `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after` `the last sitting day on which it was required to be tabled` 12 `the days on which the Legislative Assembly meets`

-- Subject to subsection (5), disallowance has the same effect as a repeal of the subordinate legislation or the specified provisions.
-- src:810 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), disallowance under this section has the same effect as a repeal of the subordinate legislation or specified provisions of it.
@ref s 63C(4) (src:810)
GIVEN `the subordinate legislation or specified provisions have been disallowed under section 63C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63C(4): the disallowance has the same effect as a repeal` MEANS
    IF `the subordinate legislation or specified provisions have been disallowed under section 63C` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- If a provision of disallowed subordinate legislation amended or repealed a provision of other subordinate legislation,
-- the disallowance revives the other provision from the date of the disallowance as if the disallowed provision had not been made.
-- src:811 | (5) If a provision of disallowed subordinate legislation (the disallowed provision) amended or repealed a provision of other subordinate legislation, the disallowance revives the other provision from the date of the disallowance as if the disallowed provision had not been made.
@ref s 63C(5) (src:811)
GIVEN `a provision of the disallowed subordinate legislation amended or repealed a provision of other subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the disallowance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 63C(5): the date from which the disallowance revives the other provision` MEANS
    IF `a provision of the disallowed subordinate legislation amended or repealed a provision of other subordinate legislation` THEN JUST `the date of the disallowance` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 64: subordinate legislation not to repeat disallowed legislation`

-- Subordinate legislation that is the same in substance or has the same effect as disallowed legislation must not be made within 6 months after the disallowance unless the Assembly rescinds the resolution.
-- src:813 | (1) This section applies if, under section 63C, the Legislative Assembly passes a resolution disallowing subordinate legislation or provisions of subordinate legislation (the disallowed legislation).
-- src:814 | (2) Subordinate legislation or provisions of subordinate legislation that is the same in substance or has the same effect as the disallowed legislation must not be made within 6 months after the disallowance unless the Legislative Assembly rescinds the resolution for disallowance.
@ref s 64(1), (2) (src:813-814)
GIVEN `the day of the disallowance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 64(2): the last day of the 6 months after the disallowance` MEANS
    `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` `the day of the disallowance` 6 `months`

@ref s 64(1), (2) (src:813-814)
GIVEN `the day of the disallowance` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the subordinate legislation is made` IS A DATE
      `it is the same in substance or has the same effect as the disallowed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Legislative Assembly has rescinded the resolution for disallowance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(2): the subordinate legislation may be made on the day` MEANS
    IF   (NOT `it is the same in substance or has the same effect as the disallowed legislation`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   `the Legislative Assembly has rescinded the resolution for disallowance`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 64(2): the last day of the 6 months after the disallowance` `the day of the disallowance`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (Day `the day on which the subordinate legislation is made` GREATER THAN Day last)

-- Subordinate legislation made in contravention of subsection (2) is of no effect.
-- src:815 | (3) Subordinate legislation or provisions of subordinate legislation made in contravention of subsection (2) is of no effect.
@ref s 64(3) (src:815)
GIVEN `it was made in contravention of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(3): the subordinate legislation is of no effect` MEANS
    IF `it was made in contravention of subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 65 to 66: what subordinate legislation may do`

DECLARE `Matter for which subordinate legislation may be made` IS ONE OF
    `a matter required or permitted to be prescribed by the Act`
    `a matter necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to the Act`
    `some other matter`

-- If an Act authorises or requires subordinate legislation under it, the power enables legislation on any matter required or permitted to be prescribed, or necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to the Act.
-- src:817 | (1) If an Act authorises or requires the making of subordinate legislation under the Act, the power enables subordinate legislation to be made with respect to any matter that:
-- src:818 | (a) is required or permitted to be prescribed by the Act; or
-- src:819 | (b) is necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to the Act.
@ref s 65(1) (src:817-819)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter for which subordinate legislation may be made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(1): the power enables subordinate legislation to be made with respect to the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `some other matter` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (1) applies even though the Act also authorises subordinate legislation for a particular purpose.
-- src:820 | (2) Subsection (1) applies even though the Act also authorises the making of subordinate legislation for a particular purpose.
@ref s 65(2) (src:820)
GIVEN `the Act also authorises the making of subordinate legislation for a particular purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(2): subsection (1) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act also authorises the making of subordinate legislation for a particular purpose`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

-- Power conferred for a particular purpose is in addition to, and does not limit the effect of, the general power unless the Act expressly provides otherwise.
-- src:821 | (3) Power conferred by the Act to make subordinate legislation for a particular purpose is in addition to, and does not limit the effect of, power conferred by the Act to make subordinate legislation under the Act unless the Act expressly provides otherwise.
@ref s 65(3) (src:821)
GIVEN `the Act expressly provides that the power for a particular purpose limits the general power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65(3): the power for a particular purpose limits the effect of the general power` MEANS
    IF `the Act expressly provides that the power for a particular purpose limits the general power` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- If an Act authorises or requires a matter to be regulated by subordinate legislation, the power may be exercised by prohibiting the matter or any aspect of it.
-- src:823 | If an Act authorises or requires a matter to be regulated by subordinate legislation, the power may be exercised by prohibiting by subordinate legislation the matter or any aspect of the matter.
@ref s 65A (src:823)
GIVEN `an Act authorises or requires the matter to be regulated by subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65A: the power may be exercised by prohibiting the matter or an aspect of it` MEANS
    IF `an Act authorises or requires the matter to be regulated by subordinate legislation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subordinate legislation may provide for the review of, or a right of appeal against, a decision made under the legislation or the Act under which it is made or in force.
-- src:825 | (1) Subordinate legislation may provide for the review of, or a right of appeal against, a decision made under the legislation or the Act under which the legislation is made or in force.
@ref s 65B(1) (src:825)
GIVEN `the decision is made under the legislation or the Act under which the legislation is made or in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65B(1): the subordinate legislation may provide for review of, or a right of appeal against, the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is made under the legislation or the Act under which the legislation is made or in force` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Body on which jurisdiction may be conferred` IS ONE OF
    `a court`
    `a tribunal`
    `a person`
    `a body that is not a court or tribunal`
    `something else that is not a court, tribunal, person or body`

-- For subsection (1), the subordinate legislation may confer jurisdiction on any court, tribunal, person or body.
-- src:826 | (2) For subsection (1), the subordinate legislation may confer jurisdiction on any court, tribunal, person or body.
@ref s 65B(2) (src:826)
GIVEN holder IS A `Body on which jurisdiction may be conferred`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65B(2): the subordinate legislation may confer jurisdiction on the holder` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `something else that is not a court, tribunal, person or body` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Thing that a power to prescribe a fee includes` IS ONE OF
    `the exemption from payment of the fee`
    `the waiver of the fee, wholly or partly`
    `the refund of the fee, wholly or partly`
    `a thing not listed`

-- A power for subordinate legislation to prescribe a fee includes power to provide for exemption from payment, waiver (wholly or partly) and refund (wholly or partly).
-- src:828 | If a power is conferred under an Act for subordinate legislation to prescribe a fee, the power includes power to provide for the following:
-- src:829 | (a) the exemption from payment of the fee;
-- src:830 | (b) the waiver (wholly or partly) of the fee;
-- src:831 | (c) the refund (wholly or partly) of the fee.
@ref s 65C (src:828-831)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that a power to prescribe a fee includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65C: the power to prescribe a fee includes power to provide for the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a thing not listed` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Thing that a power to make subordinate legislation enables for infringement notices` IS ONE OF
    `the payment of a prescribed amount instead of a penalty that may otherwise be imposed for an offence against the Act or the subordinate legislation`
    `the service of a notice relating to payment of the amount on a person alleged to have committed the offence`
    `the particulars to be included in the notice`
    `a thing not listed`

-- If an Act authorises subordinate legislation under it, the power enables legislation providing for payment of a prescribed amount instead of a penalty, service of the notice, and the particulars of the notice.
-- src:833 | If an Act authorises the making of subordinate legislation under the Act, the power enables subordinate legislation to be made providing for:
-- src:834 | (a) the payment of a prescribed amount instead of a penalty that may otherwise be imposed for an offence against the Act or the subordinate legislation; and
-- src:835 | (b) the service of a notice relating to payment of the amount on a person alleged to have committed the offence; and
-- src:836 | (c) the particulars to be included in the notice.
@ref s 65D (src:833-836)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing that a power to make subordinate legislation enables for infringement notices`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65D: the power enables subordinate legislation providing for the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a thing not listed` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- If an Act gives power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument, the instrument may require the making of a statutory declaration.
-- src:838 | (1) If an Act gives power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument, the instrument may require the making of a statutory declaration.
@ref s 65E(1) (src:838)
GIVEN `an Act gives power to make, grant or issue the statutory instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65E(1): the statutory instrument may require the making of a statutory declaration` MEANS
    IF `an Act gives power to make, grant or issue the statutory instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (1) applies whether or not the Act authorises or requires penalties to be prescribed by instrument, and if it authorises penalties not exceeding a specified amount or period of imprisonment.
-- src:839 | (2) Subsection (1) applies:
-- src:840 | (a) whether or not the Act authorises or requires penalties to be prescribed by instrument; and
-- src:841 | (b) if the Act authorises or requires penalties to be prescribed by instrument not exceeding a specified amount or period of imprisonment.
@ref s 65E(2) (src:839-841)
GIVEN `the Act authorises or requires penalties to be prescribed by instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act authorises or requires penalties not exceeding a specified amount or period of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65E(2): subsection (1) applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act authorises or requires penalties to be prescribed by instrument`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `the Act authorises or requires penalties not exceeding a specified amount or period of imprisonment`
        WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

-- If a statutory instrument substitutes an action for another being revoked at the same time, the new action is taken to have occurred after the revocation and is not ineffective because the revocation had not commenced before the substitution.
-- src:843 | (1) If the effect of a statutory instrument is to substitute an action (action A) for another action (action B) that is being revoked at the same time, action A is taken to have occurred after the revocation of action B and is therefore not ineffective by reason of the revocation not having commenced before the substitution.
@ref s 65F(1) (src:843)
GIVEN `a statutory instrument substitutes action A for action B that is being revoked at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 65F(1): action A is taken to have occurred after the revocation of action B` MEANS
    IF `a statutory instrument substitutes action A for action B that is being revoked at the same time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- If a series of actions has effect simultaneously, they are taken to have effect in the sequence that is indicated, or as the nature of the case requires.
-- Example: an instrument that revokes the appointment of a person and appoints another person to the same position is taken to have effect in sequence.
-- src:844 | (2) If a series of actions has effect simultaneously, the actions are taken to have effect in the sequence that is indicated or as the nature of the case requires.
-- src:845 | Example for section 65F
-- src:846 | A statutory instrument that revokes the appointment of a person and appoints another person to the same position is taken to have effect in sequence.
@ref s 65F(2) (src:844-846)
GIVEN `the sequence that is indicated` IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
      `the sequence that the nature of the case requires` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 65F(2): the sequence in which the actions are taken to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sequence that is indicated`
    WHEN JUST indicated THEN indicated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the sequence that the nature of the case requires`

DECLARE `Source of the matter a statutory instrument applies` IS ONE OF
    `a provision of a Territory or Commonwealth Act, or of a statutory instrument under such an Act`
    `a matter contained in any other instrument or writing`

DECLARE `Time at which the matter is taken` IS ONE OF
    `as in force at a particular time`
    `as in force from time to time`
    `as in force or existing at the time when the instrument takes effect`

-- A statutory instrument may apply, adopt or incorporate a provision of a Territory or Commonwealth Act (or of an instrument under one) as in force at a particular time or from time to time,
-- and any matter in another instrument or writing as in force or existing when the instrument takes effect;
-- but it must not, except as this section provides, apply a matter in another instrument or writing as in force or existing from time to time.
-- src:848 | Where an Act confers upon an authority power to make, grant or issue a statutory instrument, then any instrument so made, granted or issued may apply, adopt or incorporate, with or without modification:
-- src:849 | (a) the provisions of any Territory or Commonwealth Act, or of a statutory instrument under such an Act, as in force at a particular time or as in force from time to time; or
-- src:850 | (b) any matter contained in any other instrument or writing as in force or existing at the time when the first-mentioned instrument takes effect,
-- src:851 | but a statutory instrument must not, except as provided by this section, make provision for or in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating any matter contained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing from time to time.
@ref s 66 (src:848-851)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of the matter a statutory instrument applies`
      time IS A `Time at which the matter is taken`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66: the statutory instrument may apply, adopt or incorporate the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `a provision of a Territory or Commonwealth Act, or of a statutory instrument under such an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a matter contained in any other instrument or writing` THEN
        CONSIDER time
        WHEN `as in force or existing at the time when the instrument takes effect` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `as in force from time to time` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `as in force at a particular time` THEN NOTHING
